+# ArbiLend — Security Review
+
+**Scope:** `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`, `src/PriceOracle.sol`, `src/MarketProxy.sol`, `src/interfaces/*` (420 lines, commit `f138817`).
+**Target:** Arbitrum One, USDC debt, wstETH collateral at launch. weETH, ezETH, USDT next, then yield-bearing and rebasing tokens.
+**Date:** 2026-09-21
+
+**Verdict: do not deploy as-is.** In the current code, anyone can take every dollar of USDC and all deposited collateral in one transaction (C-1, C-2). They can also liquidate every borrower whenever they like (C-3). Even with access control fixed, the health-factor math (H-1) and wstETH pricing (H-2) mean honest users get liquidated well before the 80% threshold the README promises, and the liquidator gets a ~30% bonus instead of 5%.
+
+### How findings were checked
+
+- I read all the code by hand. Nothing was left out.
+- The Critical and High findings (except H-2), and L-2 and M-3, were reproduced with a throwaway Foundry proof-of-concept (PoC) outside the repo, then deleted. Each is marked **[PoC]** below. H-2 was checked against the live Arbitrum feeds instead.
+- On-chain checks (Arbitrum One, 2026-09-21):
+  - Every README address is what it says: `0x07C5…a2b7f2a` = "STETH / USD" (8 dec), `0x5083…4aD3` = "USDC / USD" (8 dec), `0x5979…0529` = wstETH, `0xaf88…5831` = native USDC.
+  - The Chainlink "wstETH-stETH Exchange Rate" feed (`0xB1552C5e96B312d0Bf8b554186F846C40614a540`) reads **1.2446**. This number drives H-2.
+
+### Severity scale
+
+| Severity | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| Critical | Anyone can steal or freeze most of the protocol's funds, with no preconditions |
+| High | Direct loss of user or protocol funds under realistic conditions |
+| Medium | Loss under specific conditions, or a hole that opens once the planned listings go live |
+| Low | Limited loss, edge cases, or hardening |
+| Info | Code quality, operations |
+
