+
+## Critical
+
+### C-1 — Anyone can upgrade the market
+
+**Where:** `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` (L84-89). Reached through `MarketProxy.fallback`.
+
+`upgradeTo` has no access control. `MarketProxy` is a UUPS-style proxy, meaning the implementation contract owns the upgrade function. So any caller can point the proxy at their own code.
+
+**What the attacker gets:** Everything, in one transaction.
+- The malicious implementation runs with the market proxy's storage and address. It sends the proxy's whole USDC balance to the attacker **[PoC: 1,000,000 USDC drained]**.
+- `CollateralVault.market` is the proxy address, so the same code can call `vault.seize(user, token, attacker, balance)` for every user and take all collateral too.
+- It can also point the proxy at a contract with no code. That bricks the market for good.
+
+**Fix:** Add `onlyOwner` to `upgradeTo`. Also:
+- Check `newImplementation.code.length > 0`.
+- Check that the new implementation reports the ERC-1967 implementation slot via `proxiableUUID()`, so a bad upgrade can't brick future upgrades.
+- Put the owner behind a multisig and timelock (L-7).
+
+Using OpenZeppelin `UUPSUpgradeable` + `Initializable` + `Ownable2Step` gives you all of this.
+
+### C-2 — Anyone can replace the oracle
+
+**Where:** `LendingMarket.setOracle` (L91-94).
+
+No `onlyOwner`.
+
+**What the attacker gets:** All USDC in the market.
+1. Deploy an oracle that prices the attacker's collateral at 1e40.
+2. Call `setOracle`.
+3. Deposit 1 wei of a listed collateral and `borrow` the whole pool **[PoC: 1 wei of collateral → 1,000,000 USDC]**.
+
+Or do the reverse: price everyone's collateral at 0 and liquidate every borrower.
+
+**Fix:** `onlyOwner`, a timelock, and ideally a sanity check that the new oracle returns a price for every listed token and the debt asset.
+
+### C-3 — Anyone can change the liquidation threshold
+
+**Where:** `LendingMarket.setLiquidationThreshold` (L96-99).
+
+No `onlyOwner` and no bounds.
+
+**What the attacker gets:**
+- Set it to `0` and every borrower's health factor becomes 0. The attacker then calls `liquidate` on every position, pays the debt, and takes the collateral at a 5% bonus. With H-2 on top, the real bonus is ~31% **[PoC: set to 0, then liquidated a 10 ETH / 1,000 USDC position that was comfortably healthy]**.
+- Set it very high and positions can be opened at ~100% LTV, which turns into bad debt on the first price dip.
+
+**Fix:** Add `onlyOwner`. Require `bps > 0 && bps < BPS`, and require it to stay below `BPS - liquidationBonus` so a liquidation can't consume more collateral than exists. Put it behind a timelock.
+
